description:
Every user needs a default Sieve script installed at provisioning time that routes mailing list traffic to List/* and lets personal email fall through to INBOX. Without this, all email lands in INBOX regardless of List-Id:.

What needs to be done:
1. Define the default Sieve script template:
     if header :contains "List-Id" "" {
       /* extract list name and fileinto List/<name> */
       fileinto "List/";
       stop;
     }
     /* else: keep in INBOX */
2. Install this script at account provisioning time (n1z4.1).
3. The List/<name> extraction must match what wcyt.3 uses for mailbox naming so the fileinto target and the auto-created mailbox name agree.
4. Allow operators to override the default script per-user via the admin CLI.
5. Add tests: Sieve evaluation of a List-Id: message routes to correct List/ mailbox; message without List-Id: goes to INBOX.
